# Shell scripts keep LF in the working tree on every platform. Git's default
# on Windows is `core.autocrlf=true`, which checks them out with CRLF, and a
# CRLF script run through `sh` fails on its own shebang — `install.sh` and
# every husky hook, including the pre-commit gate, stop working on a machine
# whose only fault was cloning with the default configuration.
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf
